    "result": "Perfect! All changes are in place. Let me create a summary of what's been implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully implemented the `--threshold` option for `frai eval` that gates CI jobs on metric quality. Here's what was added:\n\n### Core Changes (frai-core)\n\n1. **`generateReport()` enhancement** \u2013 accepts optional `thresholds` object mapping metric IDs to minimum scores (0\u20131)\n   - Evaluates each threshold: passes if metric score \u2265 minimum\n   - Missing scores fail their threshold (not crash, not pass)\n   - Report includes `passed: boolean` and `thresholds: [{metric, min, score, passed}]` only when thresholds were provided\n\n2. **Markdown reporter** \u2013 new \"Thresholds\" section showing PASS/FAIL status for each threshold\n\n3. **Test coverage** \u2013 three new tests verify passing thresholds, failing thresholds, and missing metric scores\n\n### CLI Changes (frai-cli)\n\n1. **`--threshold <metric>=<min>` option** \u2013 repeatable, validates:\n   - Format: `<metric>=<number>` (exits 2 if malformed)\n   - Range: 0\u20131 (exits 2 if outside range)\n   - Metric ID: `exact_match`, `toxicity`, `length_variance` (exits 2 with valid ID list if unknown)\n\n2. **Exit codes:**\n   - **0** \u2013 all thresholds passed, or no thresholds provided\n   - **1** \u2013 one or more thresholds failed (report still written)\n   - **2** \u2013 usage error (malformed threshold, unknown metric, invalid value)\n\n3. **Backward compatible** \u2013 without `--threshold` options, behavior is identical to before\n\n### Documentation\n\nUpdated both CLI and Core READMEs with:\n- Option syntax and valid metric IDs\n- SDK example showing threshold usage with `generateReport()`\n- Exit code behavior\n\nThe implementation works with custom metrics on the SDK side (users can define their own metrics and set thresholds for them via the Eval API).",
